The ghost is no threat. If you can *see* his bones pile, take his
stuff and run for the upstairs! That way, you'll take the previous
player's attack wands, so the & *won't* take them later and use them
against you. Then, go back to dlvl 2 or dlvl 3 to enter the mines. The
mine entrance *cannot* be located on a bones level, nor can any other
*portal level* such as Sokoban or Ludios.

You're playing a risky game if you're still at EXP:1. Even with
intrinsic speed, a single wand of striking could ruin your day. With
the extra gold from the bones, you may have enough cash to play the
run at EXP:2, which is several times easier.

And about the &? Stay the hell away from him for now. If you can,
block a corridor separating the two of you with several dust-written
Elbereths and a gold piece. That will keep him away. A key would also
help. Your speed isn't good enough; the named & may have been hastened
by a wand of speed monster back in the day, so you need *some* sort of
barrier between the two of you. Even your pet, juxtaposed between the
two of you in a corridor, could save your life.

